Package: t3v
Version: 0.2.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Server Man <dupastiy@proton.me>
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1 (>= 3.0)
Homepage: https://github.com/sureserverman/tor-v3-vanity
Source: tor-v3-vanity
Description: Tor v3 vanity .onion address generator using NVIDIA CUDA GPUs
 t3v brute-forces Ed25519 keypairs on the GPU to find .onion v3 addresses
 beginning with a chosen prefix, writing each one in Tor's
 hs_ed25519_secret_key format, named after the address it produces.
 .
 Two search kernels are available. The default "incremental" kernel computes
 one scalar multiplication per thread and then enumerates candidates by
 repeated basepoint addition with batched modular inversion, roughly 200 times
 faster than the "seed" kernel, which hashes a fresh seed per candidate and is
 kept as a reference path. Several required and bonus prefixes can be searched
 at once, and every GPU match is independently re-derived on the CPU before a
 key is written to disk.
 .
 Requires an NVIDIA GPU of compute capability 7.5 (Turing) or newer and the
 proprietary driver providing libcuda.so.1, which is not packaged here. Every
 detected CUDA device is used automatically.
